WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.300
Ho!
吼！

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.680
Ho, ho, ho.
吼，吼，吼。

10
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.800
Are you ready for some Christmas wishes?
准备好迎接圣诞愿望了吗？

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.580
Boy, am I.
天哪，我准备好了。

12
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.480
This is Season 8, Episode 10.
这是第八季第十集。

13
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.680
It was written by Mindy Kaling.
由敏迪·卡灵编剧。

14
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.480
This was her third Christmas episode, Angela.
安吉拉，这是她写的第三集圣诞特辑了。

15
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.160
I did not realize she was the go-to Christmas writer until we started this rewatch.
直到开始重温这部剧，我才意识到她是御用的圣诞编剧。

16
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:47.820
Apparently so.
看来确实如此。

17
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.200
She also wrote Diwali.
她还写过《排灯节》那一集。

18
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.020
She's like our, I guess, if it's a holiday, give it to Mindy.
她就像我们的……我想，只要是节日，就交给敏迪写吧。

19
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:54.240
Yeah.
没错。

20
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.260
This episode was also directed by Ed HelMs.
这一集还是由艾德·赫尔姆斯执导的。

21
00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.140
This was his directorial debut.
这是他的导演处女作。

22
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.560
So I would do this thing when we had a cast member who directed for the first time.
所以每当有剧组成员第一次担任导演时，我都会做一件事。

23
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.580
I would get everyone to sign the script and give it to them as a gift.
我会让所有人都在剧本上签名，然后把它作为礼物送给他们。

24
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.360
Aw.
噢。

25
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.860
Yeah, and I gave it to Ed, and he was like, Ange, I love this.
是啊，我把它送给了艾德，他说，安吉，我太喜欢这个了。

26
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.040
Well, I was not in this episode.
好吧，我没参与这一集。

27
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:20.080
I was at home with my new baby, so I did not get to participate in any of the fun stuff that happened.
当时我正带着刚出生的宝宝在家，所以没能参与其中发生的任何趣事。

28
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.060
And oh my gosh, this episode has a lot.
天哪，这一集的内容可真丰富。

29
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.780
Here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

30
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:32.240
Determined to make this the best office Christmas party ever, Andy promises to make each employee's holiday wish come true.
安迪决心举办一场史上最棒的办公室圣诞派对，他承诺要实现每位员工的节日愿望。

31
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.660
Meanwhile, Dwight and Jim are pranking one another, and someone has complained.
与此同时，德怀特和吉姆在互相恶作剧，有人对此提出了投诉。

32
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

33
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.140
Someone in their desk clump.
就是他们办公桌区域里的某个人。

34
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:43.320
Yes.
没错。

35
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.700
And Andy gives them an ultimatum.
安迪给他们下了最后通牒。

36
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.540
Yes, he does.
是的，他确实这么做了。

37
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:53.680
He says, the two of you need to stop pranking each other, or I'm going to give your Christmas bonuses to the other person.
他说，你们两个必须停止互相恶作剧，否则我就把你们的圣诞奖金给对方。

38
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:23.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

39
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:30.860
Well, listen, everyone, we are going to kick off this episode of Office Ladies with an interview with the one and only Amina Kaplan.
好了，各位，我们要用对独一无二的阿米娜·卡普兰的采访来开启本期《办公室》女士节目。

40
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.540
You know, she appeared as Val in 14 episodes of The Office, including Christmas Wishes.
你们知道，她在《办公室》的14集中饰演了瓦尔，包括《圣诞愿望》这一集。

41
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:44.420
Amina attended Tisch School of the Arts in New York, and she has won theater awards for choreography, and she can play the druMs.
阿米娜曾就读于纽约大学帝势艺术学院，她获得过戏剧编舞奖，而且还会打鼓。

42
00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:45.980
Can she play the drums?
她会打鼓吗？

43
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.640
She's like a professional drummer and now a director.
她不仅是专业鼓手，现在还是一名导演。

44
00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.940
We can't wait for you to hear this interview.
我们迫不及待想让你们听到这段采访了。

45
00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:53.540
We love her.
我们很爱她。

46
00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:53.960
Yes.
是的。

47
00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.180
So without further ado, here you go.
那么，废话不多说，请听采访。

48
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:02.100
Woo-hoo.
呜呼。

49
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:02.940
Hey, everybody.
嘿，大家好。

50
00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:03.580
What's up?
最近怎么样？

51
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.460
How y'all doing?
大家好吗？

52
00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:05.880
Oh, we're good.
噢，我们很好。

53
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.940
So good to see you.
见到你们真高兴。

54
00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.280
It's good to see you, too.
见到你我也很高兴。

55
00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.100
It's been a while.
好久不见了。

56
00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.600
It's been a hot minute, in fact.
事实上，确实有一阵子没见了。

57
00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.320
It's been a long time.
确实是很久了。

58
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:12.980
It sure has.
确实是这样。

59
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:14.360
And we're Zooming with you today.
今天我们通过Zoom和你连线。

60
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.240
You're in New Orleans?
你在新奥尔良吗？

61
00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.080
I am.
是的。

62
00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.380
This is my first time in New Orleans.
这是我第一次来新奥尔良。

63
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.660
It's awesome down here.
这里太棒了。

64
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:20.280
It's been a special place to me.
对我来说，这是一个很特别的地方。

65
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.500
I was born in Louisiana.
我出生在路易斯安那州。

66
00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.120
What?
真的吗？

67
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:28.420
Yeah, I was born in Lafayette, and I did two movies in New Orleans, and my family would come and visit.
是的，我出生在拉斐特，我在新奥尔良拍过两部电影，我的家人也会来探班。

68
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.480
And so I'm going to email you a few spots that you've got to check out.
所以我待会儿发邮件给你，推荐几个你一定要去看看的地方。

69
00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.320
I would love that, because I have the rest of my afternoon, like after 4 o'clock, I'm going to be free.
那太好了，因为我下午剩下的时间，大概4点以后，我就有空了。

70
00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:42.520
So that's all I'm going to do is just go around to spots in New Orleans, because we're working hard here.
所以我打算就在新奥尔良到处转转，因为我们在这里工作很辛苦。

71
00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.520
So we have this full schedule, although I took this hour out to hang out with you guys.
我们行程排得很满，不过我特意空出这一小时来和你们聊天。

72
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.040
Thank you.
谢谢你。

73
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.440
Oh, we love that.
噢，我们太开心了。

74
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.060
It's my pleasure.
这是我的荣幸。

75
00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:49.760
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

76
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.300
Well, we'll jump right in then.
那我们就直接开始吧。

77
00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:58.240
We're going to ask you the question that we ask every guest to kick things off, which is, how did you get your job on The Office?
我们要问你一个每个嘉宾都会被问到的开场问题：你是怎么得到《办公室》里那个角色的？

78
00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:58.940
Aha.
啊哈。

79
00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.140
Awesome casting director, Alison Jones, cast me.
是出色的选角导演艾莉森·琼斯选的我。

80
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.500
I was literally just an actor in L.A., just doing my thing.
当时我只是洛杉矶的一名普通演员，做着自己的事。

81
00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.900
And it literally just came through as a regular audition.
那个机会就像普通的试镜一样找上门来。

82
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:11.680
There it was.
机会就这样出现了。

83
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.280
Just like, boom, there's a character on a TV show.
就像是，砰的一声，电视剧里有个角色。

84
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.520
You're right for it.
你很适合这个角色。

85
00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.080
You're going to go in for that job.
你要去争取那份工作。

86
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:24.880
And it turned out to be serendipitous and special in that I was acquainted with Craig Robinson before I went into my audition.
结果证明这非常巧合且特别，因为在去试镜之前，我就认识克雷格·罗宾逊了。

87
00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.620
I did not know he was going to be at the callback.
我当时不知道他会出现在复试现场。

88
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.000
I didn't actually see him.
其实我没看到他。

89
00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.220
He saw me.
是他看到了我。

90
00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.440
If you ask Craig, Craig would be like, you don't even know, like, how much I got you on that show.
如果你去问克雷格，他会说，你根本不知道我为你争取到那个角色出了多少力。

91
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.300
So I'm like, all right, Craig, whatever I owe it to you.
所以我说，好吧，克雷格，不管怎样我都欠你一个人情。

92
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.580
So I give him the credit.
所以我把功劳归给他。

93
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.300
Like, I think Craig really was like, oh, snap, that's Amina.
我觉得克雷格当时肯定是想，噢，天哪，那是阿米娜。

94
00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:41.980
I know Amina.
我认识阿米娜。

95
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.000
And, you know, we're both musicians.
而且，你知道，我们都是音乐人。

96
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.840
And so we kind of knew each other from the music scene.
所以我们算是从音乐圈认识的。

97
00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.860
Yeah, you play drums, right?
没错，你会打鼓，对吧？

98
00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:49.600
That's right.
没错。

99
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:49.860
Yeah.
是的。

100
00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:50.560
I'm a drummer.
我是个鼓手。

101
00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:53.840
I honestly feel like that's kind of the only real thing that I am.
老实说，我觉得这大概是我唯一真正擅长的事情。

102
00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.380
I'm a hack with everything else.
除此之外我都是个半吊子。

103
00:04:55.380 --> 00:05:01.320
Because looking back at it at this age, I'm like, yeah, drumming, that's the thing that I did when I was nine years old.
因为到了这个年纪回首往事，我会想，没错，打鼓，那是我九岁时就开始做的事。

104
00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:02.720
I just was beating on stuff.
我当时就是在那儿乱敲一气。

105
00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.300
I was like hitting things and making rhythms and making beats on desktops and stuff.
我会在桌面上敲敲打打，制造节奏，打出节拍之类的。

106
00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.200
And when I was 12, a guy taught me how to play Bullet to Blue Sky by U2 on the drum set.
12岁那年，有个人教我在架子鼓上打U2乐队的《Bullet the Blue Sky》。

107
00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.020
And I was like, OK.
当时我就想，好吧。

108
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.980
And I was terrible for years and years and years because I had no training.
因为没受过专业训练，我烂了好多年好多年。

109
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.540
And my family was like, what do you think you're doing playing drums?
我家人当时就问，你以为你在打鼓是在干什么呢？

110
00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.960
And I was like, I'm doing this.
我就说，我就是在做这个。

111
00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.860
But, yeah, I'm a drummer and have been.
但没错，我是一名鼓手，一直都是。

112
00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.620
This will be a long time.
这已经是很久以前的事了。

113
00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:28.380
I'm like, this year will be 40 years of playing once I, like later this year.
我想，今年晚些时候，我就打鼓满40年了。

114
00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.400
And so, yeah, it is the only thing that I really am.
所以，没错，这确实是我唯一真正称得上是身份的事情。

115
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:31.740
Yeah.
没错。

116
00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.980
And Craig's a musician.
克雷格也是个音乐人。

117
00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.820
And we were in a band full of actors.
我们当时在一个全是演员的乐队里。

118
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.140
So if anybody got a gig, nobody was worried.
所以如果谁接到了演出，大家也不会担心。

119
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.220
It was like, OK, whatever.
就像是，好吧，随便吧。

120
00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.000
I booked the thing.
我接了个活儿。

121
00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:39.740
OK, whatever.
好吧，随便吧。

122
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.140
And Craig was friends with the guys in the band.
克雷格和乐队里的那些人是朋友。

123
00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.240
And they used to hang out.
他们以前经常一起玩。

124
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.840
And being the girl in the band, I never really hung out with them.
作为乐队里唯一的女生，我其实从来没怎么跟他们混在一起。

125
00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.120
But we were around the same scene.
但我们都在同一个圈子里。

126
00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:48.880
Right, right.
对，没错。

127
00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.180
Yeah.
没错。

128
00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.120
Oh, in my heart right now, if there ever is an office reunion,
噢，在我心里，如果《办公室》真的要重聚的话，

129
00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.180
Val's got to play the druMs.
瓦尔必须得打鼓。

130
00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.240
Val's got to boot Kevin out of the band.
瓦尔得把凯文踢出乐队。

131
00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:58.580
I know.
我知道。

132
00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.800
Was it killing you when you had to sit and listen to them play?
当你不得不坐在那儿听他们演奏时，是不是很难受？

133
00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:06.400
And you're like, I could be the drummer in Kevin in the Zits.
你当时是不是在想，我本可以成为“凯文和青春痘”乐队的鼓手。

134
00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.260
I'm not even going to mince words.
我甚至都不想委婉地说。

135
00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.360
The answer is yes.
答案是肯定的。

136
00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.160
I was standing there.
我当时就站在那儿。

137
00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.440
And I was like, you've got to be kidding me right now.
我心想，你们现在一定是在跟我开玩笑吧。

138
00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.060
They are playing drums like two feet in front of me.
他们就在我面前两英尺的地方打鼓。

139
00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.060
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

140
00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.960
Like, why am I standing here?
就像是，我为什么站在这儿？

141
00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.860
And why is Val not on the drums?
为什么瓦尔不在打鼓？

142
00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.440
Why is she not the secret killer?
为什么她不是那个隐藏的高手？

143
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.060
And, you know, it's just one of those things.
而且，你知道，这就是那种情况之一。

144
00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.020
I was the new kid.
我是个新人。

145
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.320
It was Brian's moment.
那是布莱恩的高光时刻。

146
00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.220
And it was awesome.
那真的很棒。

147
00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.940
We had the drummers at the wrong band.
我们当时把鼓手放错乐队了。

148
00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:29.820
It was just heaven.
那简直是天堂。

149
00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.440
That day was that episode was just heaven for me.
那一天，那一集对我来说简直就是天堂。

150
00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.260
And totally frustrating that I didn't speak up about being a drummer.
而且没能说出自己是鼓手这件事，也确实让人非常沮丧。

151
00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.080
I kind of kept those worlds separate.
我当时算是把这两个世界分开了。

152
00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.040
Because when I got to L.A., it was weird.
因为我刚到洛杉矶的时候，感觉很奇怪。

153
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.700
