你想知道标准与实践部门对这顶帽子有什么评价吗？

893
00:40:28.550 --> 00:40:29.250
I would love to.
我非常想知道。

894
00:40:30.150 --> 00:40:30.670
Okay.
好的。

895
00:40:31.530 --> 00:40:36.210
Well, Steve Burgess shared with me how this hard-ass hat went down.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯跟我分享了这顶“严厉”帽是怎么过审的。

896
00:40:36.210 --> 00:40:39.730
It began with an email from Standards and Practices, which said,
起初是标准与实践部门发来的一封邮件，上面写着，

897
00:40:40.270 --> 00:40:45.050
please email me a photo of the, quote, plastic butt baseball cap for my review.
请发给我一张“塑料屁股棒球帽”的照片供我审核。

898
00:40:45.530 --> 00:40:48.210
So Steve Burgess sent over two photos.
于是史蒂夫·伯吉斯发去了两张照片。

899
00:40:48.450 --> 00:40:49.610
There were two different options.
有两种不同的选择。

900
00:40:49.990 --> 00:40:52.250
And he said, here are two versions of the hat.
他说，这是两个版本的帽子。

901
00:40:52.430 --> 00:40:53.910
They're similar but different sizes.
它们很像，但尺寸不同。

902
00:40:54.430 --> 00:40:58.010
So there was one with larger buttocks and one with smaller.
所以有一个屁股比较大，另一个比较小。

903
00:40:58.430 --> 00:41:01.110
Our Standards and Practices rep was named Andrew,
我们的审查部门代表叫安德鲁，

904
00:41:01.310 --> 00:41:04.030
and Andrew had to run this all the way up to his boss.
安德鲁必须把这件事层层上报给他的老板。

905
00:41:04.030 --> 00:41:11.590
He had to take two photos of an ass hat up to his boss,
他得拿着两张屁股帽的照片去见老板，

906
00:41:11.590 --> 00:41:17.530
who said either hat was fine but wanted to know if it would be seen throughout the entire episode
老板说两顶帽子都可以，但想知道这顶帽子是会在整集里出现，

907
00:41:17.530 --> 00:41:19.750
or just in this scene in Andy's office.
还是只出现在安迪办公室的这一场戏里。

908
00:41:20.130 --> 00:41:22.330
We said it's just in this one scene.
我们说只在这一场戏里出现。

909
00:41:22.450 --> 00:41:27.250
And so the message we received was that it's okay, either hat,
于是我们收到的回复是没问题，两顶帽子选哪顶都行，

910
00:41:27.990 --> 00:41:30.130
provided it is just the one scene.
前提是只能出现在这一场戏里。

911
00:41:30.670 --> 00:41:31.790
Now, I don't know why.
现在，我不知道为什么。

912
00:41:31.910 --> 00:41:35.470
If it's approved for one scene, why can't we just see it a lot?
如果一场戏能通过审查，为什么不能多出现几次呢？

913
00:41:35.470 --> 00:41:37.330
I guess just too much.
我想可能是因为太多了吧。

914
00:41:37.470 --> 00:41:40.930
Because over time, we'll just only see asses.
因为久而久之，我们可能就只能看到屁股了。

915
00:41:41.810 --> 00:41:42.930
I guess so.
我想是吧。

916
00:41:42.930 --> 00:41:43.710
I don't know.
我不知道。

917
00:41:43.770 --> 00:41:44.590
That's so silly.
那太荒唐了。

918
00:41:44.890 --> 00:41:49.130
But they approved it for the scene, so I guess it all ended well.
但他们批准了那场戏，所以我想结果还算圆满。

919
00:41:49.270 --> 00:41:50.230
And no pixelating.
而且不用打马赛克。

920
00:41:50.430 --> 00:41:51.330
No pixelating.
不用打马赛克。

921
00:41:52.030 --> 00:41:54.290
And we could have the word ass.
我们还能用“屁股”这个词。

922
00:41:54.710 --> 00:41:55.910
We've talked about that.
我们讨论过这个问题。

923
00:41:56.030 --> 00:41:57.990
For some reason, that's an approved word.
不知为何，那是个被批准使用的词。

924
00:41:58.510 --> 00:42:01.430
What I would have loved to have seen is them say, like,
我本来很想看到他们说，比如，

925
00:42:01.570 --> 00:42:05.510
you can have the hat, but you must pixelate the crack.
你可以用那顶帽子，但必须给屁股缝打上马赛克。

926
00:42:06.330 --> 00:42:10.070
Well, we know they didn't want to see any crack in the tattoo.
嗯，我们知道他们不想在纹身上看到任何屁股缝。

927
00:42:10.370 --> 00:42:10.650
Right.
没错。

928
00:42:10.950 --> 00:42:11.590
No crack.
不能有屁股缝。

929
00:42:11.650 --> 00:42:14.610
There was a drawing of a tattoo, and they said no crack.
当时有一张纹身草图，他们说不能有屁股缝。

930
00:42:16.990 --> 00:42:18.250
Well, there you have it.
好吧，事情就是这样。

931
00:42:18.630 --> 00:42:19.510
Standards and practices.
审查部门。

932
00:42:20.450 --> 00:42:23.510
This is where Andy is going to share with Dwight and Jim
这一幕是安迪要告诉德怀特和吉姆，

933
00:42:23.510 --> 00:42:26.990
that there is someone who would like to be removed from their desk clump.
有人想从他们的办公桌区域搬走。

934
00:42:27.110 --> 00:42:29.030
They both immediately think it's each other.
他们俩立刻都以为是对方想搬走。

935
00:42:30.150 --> 00:42:31.610
And he's like, no, no, no.
安迪说，不，不，不。

936
00:42:31.910 --> 00:42:32.530
Then they know.
然后他们就明白了。

937
00:42:32.710 --> 00:42:33.170
It's Kathy.
是凯西。

938
00:42:33.330 --> 00:42:35.090
And they both whip to turn to look at her.
他们俩立刻转头看向她。

939
00:42:35.170 --> 00:42:36.270
And he's like, don't look at her.
安迪说，别看她。

940
00:42:36.590 --> 00:42:41.250
But your incessant pranking and one-upsmanship is making her crazy.
但你们没完没了的恶作剧和争强好胜让她快疯了。

941
00:42:41.250 --> 00:42:42.490
And she would like to move.
她想换个位置。

942
00:42:43.010 --> 00:42:44.190
They can't believe this.
他们简直不敢相信。

943
00:42:44.190 --> 00:42:46.290
And he goes, listen, respect the hat.
安迪说，听着，尊重一下这顶帽子。

944
00:42:46.590 --> 00:42:51.250
Take me seriously, or I'm going to give one of you your Christmas bonuses.
认真对待我，否则我就把你们其中一人的圣诞奖金给扣了。

945
00:42:51.250 --> 00:42:53.230
And you have these sizable Christmas bonuses.
你们可是有相当丰厚的圣诞奖金的。

946
00:42:53.590 --> 00:42:54.950
That gets their attention.
这下引起了他们的注意。

947
00:42:55.650 --> 00:42:56.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

948
00:42:56.510 --> 00:42:57.430
Now they know.
现在他们知道了。

949
00:42:57.530 --> 00:42:58.570
No more pranking.
不许再恶作剧了。

950
00:42:58.910 --> 00:43:01.570
Well, Andy's going to remove his hard-ass hat now
好吧，安迪现在要摘下他的“硬屁股”帽子了。

951
00:43:01.570 --> 00:43:04.150
because he was only allowed to wear it in that one scene.
因为他只在那一场戏里被允许穿它。

952
00:43:04.170 --> 00:43:08.630
But also because Jessica is arriving.
但也是因为杰西卡要来了。

953
00:43:09.030 --> 00:43:13.190
Her first stop is Erin, who gives her a big hug.
她第一站找的是艾琳，艾琳给了她一个大大的拥抱。

954
00:43:13.430 --> 00:43:13.990
Yeah.
没错。

955
00:43:14.190 --> 00:43:17.050
And Andy's like, my ex is meeting my six.
安迪当时想的是，我的前任要见我的现任了。

956
00:43:17.910 --> 00:43:18.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

957
00:43:18.950 --> 00:43:20.950
This scene is so awkward.
这一幕太尴尬了。

958
00:43:20.990 --> 00:43:23.490
I thought, it can't get more awkward than this.
我以为，不可能比这更尴尬了。

959
00:43:23.630 --> 00:43:24.710
I was wrong.
我错了。

960
00:43:25.630 --> 00:43:28.050
You were wrong because it's going to get more awkward.
你错了，因为接下来会更尴尬。

961
00:43:28.050 --> 00:43:35.810
Well, Jessica was played by Eleanor Siegler, who appears in four episodes of The Office as Andy's girlfriend, Jessica.
杰西卡由埃莉诺·西格勒饰演，她在《办公室》中出演了四集，饰演安迪的女友杰西卡。

962
00:43:36.090 --> 00:43:38.230
And she is just lovely.
她人非常好。

963
00:43:38.610 --> 00:43:48.830
The character of Jessica is just normal and brings out this very normal, calm, grounded energy in Andy.
杰西卡这个角色很正常，给安迪带来了一种非常正常、冷静、稳重的能量。

964
00:43:48.830 --> 00:43:52.090
Yeah, I really like Jessica for Andy.
是啊，我真的很喜欢杰西卡和安迪在一起。

965
00:43:52.330 --> 00:43:53.570
I'm rooting for them.
我支持他们。

966
00:43:53.570 --> 00:43:54.810
Me too.
我也是。

967
00:43:55.210 --> 00:44:02.750
Down in the warehouse, Daryl is chatting up Val and tries to casually invite her to the Christmas party.
在仓库里，达里尔正在和瓦尔聊天，并试图顺便邀请她参加圣诞派对。

968
00:44:02.750 --> 00:44:07.110
I was cracking up because the whole time, Nate thinks he's invited as well.
我当时笑得不行，因为全程内特都以为他也受邀了。

969
00:44:07.110 --> 00:44:13.850
And he's just saying the most ridiculous things that he can't wait to dress up really nice for Daryl.
他一直在说些荒唐的话，说他迫不及待想为达里尔好好打扮一番。

970
00:44:13.850 --> 00:44:17.630
Well, I would have loved to have seen more Nate upstairs at the party.
说实话，我真希望能多看到点内特在楼上参加派对的镜头。

971
00:44:17.990 --> 00:44:21.910
Me too, because it sounds like this might be his first Christmas party.
我也是，因为听起来这可能是他的第一个圣诞派对。

972
00:44:22.030 --> 00:44:22.290
Ever.
有史以来第一次。

973
00:44:23.030 --> 00:44:23.470
Yes.
是的。

974
00:44:23.810 --> 00:44:27.350
We had a fan question from Elizabeth D in Virginia who said,
我们收到了一位来自弗吉尼亚州的粉丝伊丽莎白·D的提问，她说，

975
00:44:27.590 --> 00:44:29.830
I've been waiting to ask you this for years.
这个问题我等了几年才问。

976
00:44:30.090 --> 00:44:33.510
My favorite line in The Office is in this episode when Nate says,
我在《办公室》里最喜欢的一句台词就是这一集里内特说的，

977
00:44:33.690 --> 00:44:34.770
You had me at clookies.
你用‘克鲁奇’（clookies）打动了我。

978
00:44:34.930 --> 00:44:36.730
I can't wait to find out what they are.
我迫不及待想知道那到底是什么。

979
00:44:38.730 --> 00:44:39.550
Elizabeth said,
伊丽莎白说，

980
00:44:39.690 --> 00:44:43.510
It's one of me and my brother's running bits, and we quote it to each other in different ways.
这是我和我哥哥之间的一个梗，我们经常用不同的方式互相引用。

981
00:44:43.810 --> 00:44:45.990
Please tell me how this joke came about.
请告诉我这个笑话是怎么来的。

982
00:44:46.470 --> 00:44:48.210
Well, that joke was scripted.
那个笑话是剧本里写好的。

983
00:44:48.370 --> 00:44:50.210
They did it just as it was in the script.
他们完全照着剧本演的。

984
00:44:50.210 --> 00:44:58.290
But my favorite part about this joke is actually the way Val grabs Nate's arm after he says.
但我最喜欢这个笑话的一点，其实是瓦尔在内特说完话后抓住他胳膊的方式。

985
00:44:58.810 --> 00:45:06.210
It's like when you reach over to your husband and you want him to stop talking at a dinner party or something.
就像你在晚宴上想让你丈夫闭嘴时，伸手去拉他一样。

986
00:45:06.250 --> 00:45:07.470
You're like, it's okay, babe.
你会说，没事的，亲爱的。

987
00:45:07.530 --> 00:45:08.270
It's okay.
没事的。

988
00:45:08.350 --> 00:45:09.470
You can stop now.
你可以停下来了。

989
00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:11.530
That was a great bit that Amina added to that.
那是阿米娜加进去的一个很棒的细节。

990
00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:12.670
Yeah, it was a great button.
没错，那是一个很棒的收尾。

991
00:45:13.090 --> 00:45:15.490
We also got a fan question from Neil S.
我们还收到了来自英国伦敦的粉丝尼尔·S的提问，

992
00:45:15.630 --> 00:45:17.050
in London, UK, who said,
他说，

993
00:45:17.050 --> 00:45:21.390
This scene opens with Daryl teaching Val how to use the baler,
这一幕开头是达里尔教瓦尔如何使用打包机，

994
00:45:21.530 --> 00:45:26.850
and the training seems to consist of telling her that it's capable of taking her arm or head off,
而培训内容似乎就是告诉她，这机器能把她的胳膊或头切掉，

995
00:45:26.990 --> 00:45:28.150
so exercise caution.
所以要小心。

996
00:45:28.510 --> 00:45:32.490
My question is, was this all the training that is required?
我的问题是，这就是所需的全部培训了吗？

997
00:45:32.690 --> 00:45:37.470
This is the training that Michael didn't have in order to operate the dangerous machinery?
这就是迈克尔因为没接受过培训而无法操作的危险机器吗？

998
00:45:38.170 --> 00:45:39.650
Neil, I think yes.
尼尔，我想是的。

999
00:45:39.650 --> 00:45:45.810
I think that Daryl really didn't want Michael to use the baler,
我觉得达里尔是真的不想让迈克尔用打包机，

1000
00:45:45.930 --> 00:45:51.090
and so he invented this idea that there was some elaborate training to use the baler,
所以他编造了这种说法，说操作打包机需要经过复杂的培训，

1001
00:45:51.190 --> 00:45:53.830
but really, it was just these couple of sentences.
但说真的，其实就只有那几句话而已。

1002
00:45:54.050 --> 00:45:55.150
That's what I want to believe.
我愿意相信是这样。

1003
00:45:57.070 --> 00:46:02.910
This Dwight and Jim runner is about to kick off because Dwight really sets up his whole desk area
德怀特和吉姆的这条故事线马上就要开始了，因为德怀特特意布置了他的整个办公桌区域，

1004
00:46:02.910 --> 00:46:04.570
in hopes that Jim will prank him.
就指望着吉姆能捉弄他。

1005
00:46:04.570 --> 00:46:10.790
He has an open email, he has his car keys out, so many things to entice Jim,
他打开了电子邮件，把车钥匙放在外面，摆出这么多东西来诱惑吉姆，

1006
00:46:10.950 --> 00:46:12.770
and Jim realizes really quickly,
而吉姆很快就意识到，

1007
00:46:12.970 --> 00:46:17.110
Wow, Dwight really wants my bonus, and he's trying to entrap me.
哇，德怀特是真的想要我的奖金，他这是在给我下套。

1008
00:46:17.230 --> 00:46:21.030
That means he can't drink at this party now, because when he drinks, he gets real pranky.
这意味着他现在不能在派对上喝酒了，因为他一喝酒，就特别喜欢搞恶作剧。

1009
00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:24.860
I thought that was a really funny line.
我觉得这句台词特别逗。

1010
00:46:24.980 --> 00:46:27.080
I know, I thought John as Jim was so cute saying it.
我知道，我觉得约翰演的吉姆说这话时特别可爱。

1011
00:46:27.580 --> 00:46:30.160
Andy calling out their pranking only escalated it,
安迪指出了他们的恶作剧，反而让事态升级了，

1012
00:46:30.220 --> 00:46:33.300
because now they're going to try to prank each other to get the other's bonus.
因为现在他们为了得到对方的奖金，开始互相捉弄对方了。

1013
00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:34.740
It's true.
确实如此。

1014
00:46:34.960 --> 00:46:36.260
He's kind of made it worse.
他反而把事情搞得更糟了。

1015
00:46:36.660 --> 00:46:38.160
Well, you know who is drinking?
好吧，你知道谁在喝酒吗？

1016
00:46:38.660 --> 00:46:39.440
It's Erin.
是艾琳。

1017
00:46:40.080 --> 00:46:40.460
Yes.
没错。

1018
00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:42.960
She's going to go up to Robert California at the bar,
她走到吧台找罗伯特·加州，

1019
00:46:42.960 --> 00:46:45.780
and first she's going to ask for a cola, Kirkland brand.
起初她要了一杯可乐，柯克兰品牌的。

1020
00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:47.160
And he says,
然后他说，

1021
00:46:47.420 --> 00:46:50.280
Don't you think maybe you want something stronger?
你不觉得你可能想要点更烈的东西吗？

1022
00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:52.580
You could get that soda from the kitchen.
那种汽水你在厨房就能喝到。

1023
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:52.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1024
00:46:53.380 --> 00:46:56.560
I think you came here because you want a real drink.
我觉得你来这儿是因为你想喝点真正的酒。

1025
00:46:56.560 --> 00:47:00.940
So, he pours a bunch of shots for Phyllis, Ryan, Oscar, and Kevin,
于是，他给菲利斯、瑞安、奥斯卡和凯文倒了一堆烈酒，

1026
00:47:01.120 --> 00:47:02.780
and he pours one for Erin.
也给艾琳倒了一杯。

1027
00:47:03.060 --> 00:47:05.860
And oh boy, Jiminy Christmas.
天哪，我的老天爷。

1028
00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:07.240
Jiminy Christmas indeed.
确实是我的老天爷。

1029
00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:10.620
Back in the Jim and Dwight pranking storyline,
回到吉姆和德怀特的恶作剧故事线，

1030
00:47:11.200 --> 00:47:12.480
Jim thinks he's got Dwight.
吉姆以为他抓住了德怀特。

1031
00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:14.880
He's carefully reading his credit card number.
他正仔细地念出他的信用卡号。

1032
00:47:15.040 --> 00:47:16.080
Dwight's jotting it down.
德怀特正在记下来。

1033
00:47:16.240 --> 00:47:17.320
Well, as it turns out,
结果呢，

1034
00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:21.320
Dwight buys Pam a $200 bouquet of flowers.
德怀特给帕姆买了一束价值200美元的花。

1035
00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:22.820
Yes.
没错。

1036
00:47:23.020 --> 00:47:23.540
$200.
200美元。

1037
00:47:23.960 --> 00:47:25.440
That's going to be a big-ass bouquet.
那得是一大束花啊。

1038
00:47:26.460 --> 00:47:27.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1039
00:47:27.420 --> 00:47:30.040
I think she deserves it because, like I said,
我觉得她值得，因为就像我说的，

1040
00:47:30.180 --> 00:47:33.140
Jim's going to be doing a lot of out-of-office extracurriculars.
吉姆接下来会有很多办公室之外的额外活动。

1041
00:47:33.440 --> 00:47:34.380
I thought you would say that.
我就知道你会这么说。

1042
00:47:35.040 --> 00:47:37.160
Val is now going to arrive to the party.
瓦尔现在要来参加派对了。

1043
00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:38.400
She looks stunning.
她看起来美极了。

1044
00:47:38.660 --> 00:47:40.560
She is in a beautiful gown,
她穿着一件漂亮的礼服，

1045
00:47:40.740 --> 00:47:44.140
like a floor-length purple off-shoulder gown.
就像那种拖地的紫色露肩礼服。

1046
00:47:45.040 --> 00:47:47.520
Yes, we talked with Amina about this.
是的，我们和阿米娜聊过这个。

1047
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:51.480
This is all because Daryl said people dress up for the Christmas party,
这全是因为达里尔说大家参加圣诞派对都会盛装打扮，

1048
00:47:51.480 --> 00:47:53.240
and she took it quite literally.
而她把它当真了。

1049
00:47:53.960 --> 00:47:55.720
I have a catch in this scene,
这一幕里我有个槽点，

1050
00:47:55.740 --> 00:47:58.200
and it's about how someone is dressed,
是关于某人的穿着的，

1051
00:47:58.240 --> 00:47:59.260
and it's not Val,
而且那不是瓦尔，

1052
00:47:59.400 --> 00:48:00.520
but it's in this scene.
但它出现在这一幕里。

1053
00:48:00.720 --> 00:48:01.840
Look at what I wrote down.
看看我写下的东西。

1054
00:48:02.680 --> 00:48:04.380
What is Kathy's skirt?
凯西的裙子是什么样的？

1055
00:48:04.820 --> 00:48:05.420
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1056
00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:06.220
What is her skirt?
她的裙子是什么样的？

1057
00:48:06.220 --> 00:48:08.180
It looks like something that, like,
看起来就像是那种，怎么说呢，

1058
00:48:08.440 --> 00:48:11.760
a kid made in, like, a sewing class.
小孩子在缝纫课上做出来的东西。

1059
00:48:11.760 --> 00:48:13.380
Okay, I know what you're talking about.
好吧，我知道你在说什么了。

1060
00:48:13.460 --> 00:48:14.520
For, like, a theater production.
就像是那种戏剧演出用的。

1061
00:48:14.520 --> 00:48:19.220
And it has this giant, crazy, like, elastic band.
而且它还有那种巨大的、疯狂的松紧带。

1062
00:48:19.820 --> 00:48:22.400
As you said it, I knew exactly what you meant.
你一说我就完全明白你的意思了。

1063
00:48:22.720 --> 00:48:26.900
Immediately, it looks like when my sister took a sewing class.
立刻就想到了我妹妹上缝纫课时的样子。

1064
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:30.000
Yes, it's like the first skirt you learn to make.
没错，就像是你学会做的第一条裙子。

1065
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.860
You learn to make, yeah.
你学会做的，对。

1066
00:48:31.080 --> 00:48:34.400
There's no zipper on it because zippers are intermediate sewing.
上面没有拉链，因为拉链属于中级缝纫技术。

1067
00:48:35.200 --> 00:48:39.140
Yeah, it's a stinker, I'm going to say it.
是啊，这裙子真够烂的，我得直说。

1068
00:48:39.260 --> 00:48:39.880
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1069
00:48:40.320 --> 00:48:42.020
Maybe when we get to interview Lindsay,
也许等我们采访琳赛的时候，

1070
00:48:42.020 --> 00:48:46.520
we'll ask her about this skirt because, um, wowser.
我们会问她关于这条裙子的事，因为，嗯，真是绝了。

1071
00:48:46.920 --> 00:48:49.980
In the conference room, Erin is really holding court now.
在会议室里，艾琳现在真的是全场的焦点。

1072
00:48:50.140 --> 00:48:52.440
She is buzzed and doing impressions.
她喝高了，正在模仿别人。

1073
00:48:53.300 --> 00:48:54.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1074
00:48:54.180 --> 00:48:58.060
She's doing a pretty darn good impression of Stanley to his delight.
她模仿斯坦利的水平相当不错，斯坦利本人也很开心。

1075
00:48:58.060 --> 00:48:59.800
Yeah, he's very tickled by it.
是啊，他被逗得很乐呵。

1076
00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:04.080
But all of this is going to end when Dwight starts screaming.
但这一切都会在德怀特尖叫时结束。

1077
00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:06.220
He's screaming that he's been attacked.
他在尖叫说自己被袭击了。

1078
00:49:06.740 --> 00:49:11.400
And we find a porcupine in his drawer that he says,
然后我们在他的抽屉里发现了一只豪猪，他说，

1079
00:49:11.660 --> 00:49:13.120
clearly, Jim has put there.
很明显，是吉姆放进去的。

1080
00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:14.200
Yes.
没错。

1081
00:49:14.600 --> 00:49:18.160
Dwight is going to claim that his hand is lacerated,
德怀特声称他的手被割伤了，

1082
00:49:18.300 --> 00:49:19.280
that he has been quilled,
说他被扎了刺，

1083
00:49:19.300 --> 00:49:22.720
and he's going to tell Andy that Jim is to blame for this porcupine.
而且他还要告诉安迪，这只豪猪是吉姆干的好事。

1084
00:49:22.940 --> 00:49:25.420
But Jim is going to very clearly state,
但吉姆会非常明确地指出，

1085
00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:28.660
um, I'm sorry, but of this whole group of people,
嗯，抱歉，但在这一群人里，

1086
00:49:28.880 --> 00:49:32.720
who do you think would have access to a porcupine?
你觉得谁能弄到一只豪猪？

1087
00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:34.340
It's clearly Dwight.
显然是德怀特。

1088
00:49:35.380 --> 00:49:39.120
Yes, and Dwight ends up revealing that the porcupine's name is Henrietta.
是的，最后德怀特透露这只豪猪的名字叫亨丽埃塔。

1089
00:49:39.560 --> 00:49:41.700
We got a lot of fan mail about this porcupine.
我们收到了很多关于这只豪猪的粉丝来信。

1090
00:49:41.840 --> 00:49:42.260
Jess C.
来自澳大利亚悉尼的杰斯·C

1091
00:49:42.360 --> 00:49:43.700
from Sydney, Australia said,
问道，

1092
00:49:43.840 --> 00:49:45.780
where did you guys get Henrietta from?
你们是从哪儿弄来的亨丽埃塔？

1093
00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:48.500
How much does it cost to rent a porcupine?
租一只豪猪要花多少钱？

1094
00:49:48.600 --> 00:49:52.000
And are there any special considerations or safety meetings
和豪猪一起工作时，有什么特别的注意事项

1095
00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:54.020
for working with a porcupine?
或者安全会议吗？

1096
00:49:54.580 --> 00:49:57.540
Well, Jess, as with most animals we used on the office,
嗯，杰斯，和我们在《办公室》里用过的绝大多数动物一样，

1097
00:49:57.720 --> 00:50:00.460
our porcupine came through Bob Dunn's Animal Services.
我们的豪猪是通过鲍勃·邓恩动物服务公司找来的。

1098
00:50:00.860 --> 00:50:04.820
The porcupine cost $1,500 for one day of work.
这只豪猪一天的租金是1500美元。

1099
00:50:04.820 --> 00:50:08.280
That included the cost of the animal and two trainers
这包括了动物本身的费用、两名驯兽师，

1100
00:50:08.280 --> 00:50:11.920
and the animal's transportation to and from the set.
以及动物往返片场的交通费。

1101
00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:13.580
And Steve Burgess says,
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，

1102
00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:16.520
we always have safety meetings when we're working with animals.
我们和动物一起工作时总是会开安全会议。

1103
00:50:16.700 --> 00:50:18.800
It didn't matter what animal, even if it was a dog.
不管是什么动物，哪怕是狗也一样。

1104
00:50:18.800 --> 00:50:23.260
And the rules to keep animals and crews safe are really strict.
而且保护动物和工作人员安全的规定非常严格。

1105
00:50:23.540 --> 00:50:27.420
And Steve Burgess told me that the trainers worked with Rain before the scene
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，驯兽师在拍摄前和雷恩一起工作过，

1106
00:50:27.420 --> 00:50:31.380
to instruct him on how exactly to handle the porcupine
指导他具体该如何处理豪猪，

1107
00:50:31.380 --> 00:50:33.480
without hurting himself or the animal.
以免伤到自己或动物。

1108
00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:35.560
Now, I was not there,
当时我不在场，

1109
00:50:35.720 --> 00:50:39.640
but Angela, you emailed me pictures of the porcupine.
但安吉拉，你给我发过豪猪的照片。

1110
00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:40.340
I did.
是的，我发过。

1111
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:41.780
Okay, so here's the thing.
好吧，情况是这样的。

1112
00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:44.000
I have such a clear memory of this day.
我对那天记忆犹新。

1113
00:50:44.480 --> 00:50:45.420
Next to Rain,
除了雷恩，

1114
00:50:45.580 --> 00:50:48.660
I'm the person standing closest to the porcupine.
我是离豪猪最近的人。

1115
00:50:48.780 --> 00:50:53.880
So I was very aware that I wanted to keep my movements very minimal.
所以我非常清楚自己得尽量减少动作。

1116
00:50:53.880 --> 00:50:57.720
And I found in my digital email clutter,
我在杂乱的电子邮箱里找到了，

1117
00:50:58.060 --> 00:51:01.320
an email I sent to Ed and Rain.
一封我发给埃德和雷恩的邮件。

1118
00:51:01.580 --> 00:51:04.740
I took a picture of Rain holding the porcupine.
我拍了一张雷恩抱着豪猪的照片。

1119
00:51:04.900 --> 00:51:07.220
And Ed is standing right behind him.
埃德就站在他身后。

1120
00:51:07.320 --> 00:51:08.360
It's a great picture.
那是一张很棒的照片。

1121
00:51:08.920 --> 00:51:11.560
And Rain is wearing in the photo,
照片里的雷恩戴着，

1122
00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:17.040
these massive, long, thick leather gloves.
那种又大又长又厚的皮手套。

1123
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:19.860
They were specially given to him to hold her.
那是专门给他准备的，用来抱它。

1124
00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:21.920
And he was shown how to hold her.
而且有人教过他该怎么抱它。

1125
00:51:21.920 --> 00:51:23.960
And her name, in my email,
在我的邮件里，它的名字，

1126
00:51:24.240 --> 00:51:27.480
I say, here's a photo of you guys with Penelope.
我说，这是你们和佩内洛普的合影。

1127
00:51:28.380 --> 00:51:30.640
Oh, Henrietta's real name is Penelope.
哦，亨丽埃塔的真名是佩内洛普。

1128
00:51:30.780 --> 00:51:31.140
Yes.
是的。

1129
00:51:31.540 --> 00:51:33.440
These are the cutest names, by the way.
顺便说一句，这些名字太可爱了。

1130
00:51:33.740 --> 00:51:36.820
And also, the other memory I have of her
另外，我对它的另一个记忆是，

1131
00:51:36.820 --> 00:51:40.020
is that she loved a snack.
它特别喜欢吃零食。

1132
00:51:40.200 --> 00:51:43.140
And they would give her stuff to snack on in that drawer.
他们会把零食放在那个抽屉里给它吃。

1133
00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:44.260
So she had a carrot.
所以它吃过胡萝卜。

1134
00:51:44.460 --> 00:51:46.520
I think she had a corn on the cob.
我想它还吃过玉米棒。

1135
00:51:46.700 --> 00:51:48.460
But she loved her snacks.
但它真的很爱吃零食。

1136
00:51:48.460 --> 00:51:50.740
And they kept her very calm and happy.
这让它保持得非常冷静和快乐。

1137
00:51:50.740 --> 00:51:55.440
Well, you know, if you do get stung by a porcupine quill,
嗯，你知道，如果你真的被豪猪刺扎到了，

1138
00:51:55.580 --> 00:51:58.760
because, you know, people think that they shoot their quills at you,
因为你知道，人们以为它们会向你发射刺，

1139
00:51:58.840 --> 00:51:59.360
but they don't.
但其实它们不会。

1140
00:51:59.440 --> 00:52:00.740
It's more like a bee sting,
这更像蜜蜂蜇人，

1141
00:52:00.900 --> 00:52:03.840
where they'll whip their tail and they'll, like, thwap you.
它们会甩动尾巴，然后“啪”地一下抽在你身上。

1142
00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:06.160
Jenna, did you do some Googling, Jenna?
珍娜，你是不是去谷歌搜索过了，珍娜？

1143
00:52:06.660 --> 00:52:08.700
No, I just know a lot about porcupines.
不，我只是对豪猪了解很多而已。

1144
00:52:08.820 --> 00:52:10.000
You are full of it.
你满嘴胡言。

1145
00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:11.580
Of course I did some Googling.
我当然去谷歌搜索过了。

1146
00:52:12.700 --> 00:52:13.420
Of course.
当然了。

1147
00:52:13.420 --> 00:52:17.700
So what happens if you get whapped with a porcupine tail and you get quilled?
那么，如果被豪猪尾巴抽到并被刺扎了会怎样？

1148
00:52:17.820 --> 00:52:18.360
What do you do?
该怎么办？

1149
00:52:18.620 --> 00:52:22.640
A quill becomes more anchored in the skin the longer they're there.
刺在皮肤里待的时间越长，扎得就越深。

1150
00:52:22.800 --> 00:52:24.640
They have these little barbs.
它们上面有这种小倒钩。

1151
00:52:24.820 --> 00:52:29.860
Like, it's very common, actually, for dogs to get quilled by a porcupine,
其实，狗被豪猪刺扎到是非常普遍的现象，

1152
00:52:29.920 --> 00:52:32.700
because they'll kind of stick their nose down and then they'll get quilled.
因为它们会把鼻子凑过去，然后就被扎到了。

1153
00:52:32.700 --> 00:52:37.420
The body heat of whoever has been quilled, a human or a dog,
无论是被扎的是人还是狗，体温都会导致刺膨胀，

1154
00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:43.500
it causes them to expand and also burrow into your skin.
并进一步钻进皮肤里。

1155
00:52:43.680 --> 00:52:46.800
And they can even migrate, like, all the way to your organs.
它们甚至会游走到你的器官里。

1156
00:52:46.980 --> 00:52:47.360
Stop it.
别说了。

1157
00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:48.480
And you can die.
而且人可能会因此丧命。

1158
00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:49.420
It's very dangerous.
这非常危险。

1159
00:52:49.420 --> 00:52:56.040
And so you need to go to a doctor or take your dog to a vet to be de-quilled
所以你需要去看医生，或者带你的狗去兽医那里拔刺，

1160
00:52:56.040 --> 00:53:00.220
because you don't want to leave any of the barb in there at all.
因为你绝对不想让任何倒钩残留在里面。

1161
00:53:00.220 --> 00:53:05.860
Sometimes they even have to do, like, a CT scan to make sure that no quill edges broke off.
有时甚至需要做CT扫描，以确保没有断掉的刺尖留在体内。

1162
00:53:06.020 --> 00:53:07.240
That is fascinating.
太神奇了。

1163
00:53:07.860 --> 00:53:08.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1164
00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:10.060
Yeah, you don't want to get quilled.
是啊，你可不想被豪猪刺扎到。

1165
00:53:10.140 --> 00:53:12.720
And porcupines have up to 30,000 quills.
豪猪身上有多达三万根刺。

1166
00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:13.320
Wow.
哇。

1167
00:53:13.560 --> 00:53:14.260
30,000.
三万根。

1168
00:53:14.660 --> 00:53:15.120
Wow.
哇。

1169
00:53:15.560 --> 00:53:19.100
I can tell you Penelope was really chill and she had the sweetest little face
我可以告诉你，佩内洛普非常冷静，她有一张最可爱的小脸，

1170
00:53:19.100 --> 00:53:21.920
and she just would hang out and gnaw on her carrot for the most part.
大多数时候她就待在那儿啃胡萝卜。

1171
00:53:22.500 --> 00:53:24.060
They're very sweet animals.
它们是非常可爱的动物。

1172
00:53:24.480 --> 00:53:28.480
We should also mention the storyline that's happening in the background of this scene
我们还应该提一下这个场景背景中发生的故事线，

1173
00:53:28.480 --> 00:53:34.300
is that Toby says that a lot of this reminds him of a plot of his latest Chad Flinderman novel,
托比说这一切让他想起了他最新一部查德·弗林德曼小说里的情节，

1174
00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:35.480
A Murder for Framing.
《陷害谋杀案》。

1175
00:53:36.740 --> 00:53:37.560
All of it.
全部都是。

1176
00:53:37.780 --> 00:53:40.760
All of Toby's writing cracks me up.
托比写的所有东西都让我笑个不停。

1177
00:53:40.900 --> 00:53:45.960
I could have seen, like, a whole episode dedicated to his, like, one of his novels.
我甚至能想象出一整集专门讲他其中一部小说的内容。

1178
00:53:46.700 --> 00:53:49.040
Erin has moved from impressions to dancing.
艾琳已经从模仿秀转为跳舞了。

1179
00:53:49.640 --> 00:53:51.120
What is this dancing?
这是什么舞？

1180
00:53:51.360 --> 00:53:55.180
What is this backward scooch with her elbow going up, up, up, up, up?
这种一边向后挪，一边手肘向上、向上、向上、向上、向上抬的动作是什么？

1181
00:53:55.180 --> 00:53:57.000
I was like, Ellie, what are you doing?
当时我就想，艾莉，你在干什么？

1182
00:53:57.220 --> 00:53:58.640
I laughed so hard.
我笑得好厉害。

1183
00:53:58.640 --> 00:54:00.100
I forgot this dance.
我都忘了这段舞了。

1184
00:54:00.480 --> 00:54:02.480
We got a fan question from Razel L.
我们收到一个来自拉泽尔·L的粉丝提问，

1185
00:54:02.660 --> 00:54:05.380
in me and Ellie's hometown of St. Louis, Missouri,
她来自我和艾莉的家乡密苏里州圣路易斯，

1186
00:54:05.380 --> 00:54:06.460
who said,
她说，

1187
00:54:06.780 --> 00:54:09.640
I've always loved Ellie's dance moves in this episode.
我一直很喜欢艾莉在这一集里的舞步。

1188
00:54:09.840 --> 00:54:14.200
Were there specific descriptions of the dance moves in the script or was this all Ellie?
剧本里对舞步有具体的描述吗，还是全靠艾莉自己发挥？

1189
00:54:14.540 --> 00:54:15.760
This was all Ellie.
这全靠艾莉自己。

1190
00:54:15.980 --> 00:54:19.340
I looked in the script to see the scene description because, you know,
我查了剧本想看看场景描述，因为你知道，

1191
00:54:19.340 --> 00:54:23.060
sometimes they did give us very specific action.
有时候他们确实会给我们非常具体的动作指导。

1192
00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:25.360
But this is what it said.
但剧本上是这么写的。

1193
00:54:25.540 --> 00:54:25.860
It said,
上面写着，

1194
00:54:26.080 --> 00:54:29.480
Dwight, Ryan, Kelly, Kathy, and Phyllis are in a dance circle.
德怀特、瑞安、凯莉、凯西和菲利斯在跳舞圈里。

1195
00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:31.340
Erin is in the center.
艾琳在中间。

1196
00:54:31.700 --> 00:54:33.260
She is dancing up a storm.
她跳得非常疯狂。

1197
00:54:33.520 --> 00:54:34.540
Her hair is down.
她的头发披散着。

1198
00:54:34.820 --> 00:54:36.200
Face is a little sweaty.
脸上有点汗。

1199
00:54:36.380 --> 00:54:39.460
But the dancing was, guys, that was all Ellie.
但伙计们，那段舞完全是艾莉自己跳的。

1200
00:54:39.640 --> 00:54:42.160
Ellie, you get some applause for those dance moves.
艾莉，你得为那些舞步赢得一些掌声。

1201
00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:42.580
For sure.
当然。

1202
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:46.020
That backwards elbow thing, I will never forget.
那个反向手肘的动作，我永远忘不了。

1203
00:54:46.020 --> 00:54:48.180
And I kind of want to recreate it with you.
而且我有点想和你一起重现那个动作。

1204
00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:53.220
I have to say, I really love the detail that Erin's hair starts up kind of looking nice.
我必须说，我真的很喜欢艾琳的头发一开始看起来还不错的细节。

1205
00:54:53.400 --> 00:54:58.300
And then throughout the episode, it comes down and it gets frizzier and more frazzled.
然后随着剧集推进，她的头发散了下来，变得越来越毛躁、越来越凌乱。

1206
00:54:58.660 --> 00:55:01.400
And she gets sweatier as she gets drunker.
而且她越喝越醉，汗也出得越多。

1207
00:55:01.940 --> 00:55:04.660
Angela, do you remember our friend that we have in common?
安吉拉，你还记得我们共同的那位朋友吗？

1208
00:55:04.820 --> 00:55:07.040
And I won't say who it is because I won't embarrass her.
我不会说是谁，因为我不想让她难堪。

1209
00:55:07.260 --> 00:55:09.420
But we were all at a party together.
但我们当时都在同一个聚会上。

1210
00:55:09.680 --> 00:55:13.480
And then like throughout the party, she got drunker and her hair kept getting bigger
然后随着聚会的进行，她喝得越来越醉，头发也变得越来越大

1211
00:55:13.480 --> 00:55:15.280
and bigger and bigger and bigger.
越来越大，越来越大，越来越大。

1212
00:55:15.480 --> 00:55:17.440
And I have pictures from the night.
我还有那天晚上的照片呢。

1213
00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:18.700
Yes, yes, I do.
是的，是的，我记得。

1214
00:55:19.040 --> 00:55:19.960
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1215
00:55:20.020 --> 00:55:22.340
If she's listening, she knows exactly who she is.
如果她在听的话，她完全知道我说的是谁。

1216
00:55:22.360 --> 00:55:23.140
She knows who she is.
她知道她是谁。

1217
00:55:23.260 --> 00:55:23.840
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1218
00:55:23.840 --> 00:55:24.560
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1219
00:55:26.860 --> 00:55:32.920
Well, I was actually in the scene with Jessica and Andy.
其实当时我和杰西卡还有安迪在那场戏里。

1220
00:55:33.220 --> 00:55:38.160
You know, Angela's standing there with them when Erin does this back scooch dance move
你知道，当艾琳跳那个后退滑步舞的时候，安吉拉就站在他们旁边

1221
00:55:38.160 --> 00:55:41.560
and then says by the end of the night, she hopes to see them kiss.
然后她说希望在晚上结束前看到他们接吻。

1222
00:55:41.720 --> 00:55:44.260
And then she squeezes their heads together.
接着她把他们的头挤在一起。

1223
00:55:44.600 --> 00:55:46.800
I was standing right there.
我就站在那儿。

1224
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:48.580
It was so awkward.
太尴尬了。

1225
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:50.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1226
00:55:50.440 --> 00:55:52.800
And it was just as awkward to rewatch it.
重看的时候也一样尴尬。

1227
00:55:53.060 --> 00:55:56.820
And when she leaves, that's when Jessica goes, that's who you dated?
当她离开时，杰西卡就说，那就是你约会过的对象？

1228
00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:58.300
That's the girl you dated?
那就是你约会过的女孩？

1229
00:55:59.080 --> 00:56:01.920
And Andy's like, yeah, I mean, she's normally not like this.
安迪说，是啊，我的意思是，她平时不是这样的。

1230
00:56:01.920 --> 00:56:06.380
But I thought Eleanor delivered so many great moments in this episode.
但我认为埃莉诺在这一集中贡献了很多精彩的瞬间。

1231
00:56:06.540 --> 00:56:07.460
And that's one of them.
而那正是其中之一。

1232
00:56:08.180 --> 00:56:09.260
Well, why don't we take a break?
好吧，我们休息一下怎么样？

1233
00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:12.580
Because next up, Erin is going to tell Andy her Christmas wish.
因为接下来，艾琳要告诉安迪她的圣诞愿望了。

1234
00:56:12.720 --> 00:56:13.880
And it's a doozy.
那可真是个重磅炸弹。

1235
00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:15.120
It's so horrible.
太可怕了。

1236
00:56:15.320 --> 00:56:16.940
How do you come back from that?
这要怎么收场啊？

1237
00:56:17.340 --> 00:56:18.360
I don't know.
我不知道。

1238
00:56:28.250 --> 00:56:29.150
We're back.
我们回来了。

1239
00:56:29.310 --> 00:56:32.350
And Andy goes in the conference room basically to check on Erin.
安迪走进会议室，基本上是为了看看艾琳的情况。

1240
00:56:32.610 --> 00:56:34.850
He's like, hey, I think you should eat something.
他说，嘿，我觉得你应该吃点东西。

1241
00:56:35.550 --> 00:56:37.310
And she tells him her holiday wish.
然后她告诉了他她的节日愿望。

1242
00:56:37.610 --> 00:56:43.190
And it's for Jessica to be dead, like in the ground with worms coming out of her.
她的愿望是让杰西卡死掉，就像躺在土里、身上爬满虫子那样。

1243
00:56:43.390 --> 00:56:47.190
And Andy gets really angry and says, you know what?
安迪非常生气，说，你知道吗？

1244
00:56:47.350 --> 00:56:47.930
Take it back.
把这话收回去。

1245
00:56:48.070 --> 00:56:48.850
That's my girlfriend.
那是我女朋友。

1246
00:56:49.210 --> 00:56:49.770
Take it back.
把这话收回去。

1247
00:56:50.010 --> 00:56:52.230
And Erin's like, no, you promised.
艾琳却说，不，你答应过的。

1248
00:56:52.430 --> 00:56:54.870
So what are you, a liar or a murderer?
所以你到底是个骗子，还是个杀人犯？

1249
00:56:55.210 --> 00:56:58.390
And everyone is witness to this moment, to this argument.
每个人都目睹了这一刻，目睹了这场争吵。

1250
00:56:58.590 --> 00:57:04.110
And I'm thinking, if you're Jessica standing right outside the partition there, that glass,
我在想，如果你是杰西卡，就站在隔断外面那块玻璃后面，

1251
00:57:04.110 --> 00:57:05.130
you're watching this.
你正在看这一幕。

1252
00:57:05.290 --> 00:57:06.910
You can probably hear it.
你大概能听到声音。

1253
00:57:07.230 --> 00:57:09.190
How are you not like, you know what?
你怎么会没有那种感觉呢，你知道吗？

1254
00:57:09.510 --> 00:57:10.230
F*** this.
去他妈的。

1255
00:57:10.310 --> 00:57:11.050
I'm out of here.
我不干了。

1256
00:57:11.370 --> 00:57:12.950
Like, she wants me dead.
就好像，她想让我死一样。

1257
00:57:13.110 --> 00:57:15.370
I'm not going to stay and hang out at this party.
我才不会留下来参加这个派对。

1258
00:57:16.330 --> 00:57:17.250
I don't know.
我不知道。

1259
00:57:17.410 --> 00:57:24.050
I kind of believe that maybe the music makes it hard to hear around the door and out in
我有点相信，也许是因为音乐声太大，让人听不清门外和外面……

1260
00:57:24.050 --> 00:57:25.990
That's what you have to believe, right?
你只能这么想，对吧？

1261
00:57:26.350 --> 00:57:26.810
Yes.
没错。

1262
00:57:27.170 --> 00:57:30.470
But I'm going to tell you what my favorite part of this scene was.
但我得告诉你，这一幕里我最喜欢的部分是什么。

1263
00:57:31.270 --> 00:57:35.010
It's the people dancing in the background.
是背景里跳舞的人。

1264
00:57:37.110 --> 00:57:44.630
Because their dancing starts to kind of slowly disintegrate as the argument escalates.
因为随着争吵升级，他们的舞姿开始慢慢变得支离破碎。

1265
00:57:45.250 --> 00:57:47.510
It is so fun.
太好玩了。

1266
00:57:47.550 --> 00:57:50.370
I watched it both with and without sound.
我开了声音和关了声音各看了一遍。

1267
00:57:50.370 --> 00:57:51.190
I don't know.
我不知道。

1268
00:57:51.350 --> 00:57:52.930
I was so tickled by it.
我被逗乐了。

1269
00:57:53.150 --> 00:57:55.290
Everyone's just like dancing their heart out.
每个人都跳得非常卖力。

1270
00:57:55.290 --> 00:58:00.110
And then slowly, ever so slowly, by the end, they're just standing there staring.
然后慢慢地，非常缓慢地，到最后，他们就站在那儿盯着看。

1271
00:58:00.350 --> 00:58:01.870
And it's chef's kiss.
简直绝了。

1272
00:58:02.770 --> 00:58:03.250
Okay.
好吧。

1273
00:58:03.250 --> 00:58:04.130
I'll look for it.
我会留意一下的。

1274
00:58:04.590 --> 00:58:09.150
Well, now Phyllis is going to tell Val that she thinks she looks like a princess and says,
好了，现在菲利斯要告诉瓦尔，她觉得她看起来像个公主，并说，

1275
00:58:09.290 --> 00:58:11.090
don't listen to what everyone else is saying.
别听别人怎么说。

1276
00:58:11.270 --> 00:58:13.950
It's one of those backhanded compliments, right?
这算是一种反讽的恭维，对吧？

1277
00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:14.670
Yes.
是的。

1278
00:58:14.850 --> 00:58:15.050
Yes.
没错。

1279
00:58:15.050 --> 00:58:20.090
And this is the scene Amina was talking about in our interview because they gave Phyllis
这就是阿米娜在采访中提到的那一幕，因为他们给了菲利斯

1280
00:58:20.090 --> 00:58:22.470
a whole bunch of alts, like in the moment, right?
一大堆备选台词，就在那一刻，对吧？

1281
00:58:22.710 --> 00:58:25.430
These one-liners to go up to Val and say.
这些用来走向瓦尔并说出的俏皮话。

1282
00:58:25.830 --> 00:58:28.190
And there are a bunch in the bloopers.
花絮里还有很多。

1283
00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:33.670
But what is going to happen is Daryl is going to clock this, right?
但接下来会发生的是，达里尔会注意到这一点，对吧？

1284
00:58:33.990 --> 00:58:34.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1285
00:58:34.550 --> 00:58:36.790
He's got to step up to the plate here for her.
他必须在这里为她挺身而出。

1286
00:58:37.350 --> 00:58:39.670
And he's going to do the cutest thing, but we'll get to it.
他会做一件最可爱的事，但我们待会儿再说。

1287
00:58:39.670 --> 00:58:39.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1288
00:58:40.490 --> 00:58:46.670
Jim is now going to approach Andy and Oscar and Jessica and Phyllis, and he's going to
吉姆现在要走近安迪、奥斯卡、杰西卡和菲利斯，他要

1289
00:58:46.670 --> 00:58:50.250
show them a vandalized photo of Cece.
给他们看一张被涂鸦的西西的照片。

1290
00:58:50.490 --> 00:58:52.410
He's trying to set Dwight up.
他想陷害德怀特。

1291
00:58:52.610 --> 00:58:56.090
I went to the shooting draft because I was curious to see how it was described.
我查了拍摄剧本，因为我很好奇它是怎么描述的。

1292
00:58:56.570 --> 00:58:59.450
It says, Jim shows them a photo of Cece.
上面写着，吉姆给他们看了一张西西的照片。

1293
00:58:59.670 --> 00:59:01.690
It has been defaced with a Sharpie.
照片被马克笔涂花了。

1294
00:59:01.890 --> 00:59:05.790
She has a handlebar mustache, a goatee, and devil's horns.
她长了八字胡、山羊胡，还有恶魔角。

1295
00:59:06.490 --> 00:59:08.470
Oscar is incensed.
奥斯卡气疯了。

1296
00:59:08.470 --> 00:59:15.350
And let me tell you, if you go to the bloopers for this, there is one take where Oscar has
我跟你说，如果你去看这一段的花絮，有一个镜头里奥斯卡的

1297
00:59:15.350 --> 00:59:18.250
a reaction that is so hilarious, everyone breaks.
反应太搞笑了，所有人都笑场了。

1298
00:59:18.450 --> 00:59:21.210
It reminded me, Jen, of when he did unbelievable.
这让我想起了，珍，他做那个“难以置信”表情的时候。

1299
00:59:22.290 --> 00:59:27.850
But I want to put it in our stories because he does this thing, like it won't play here,
但我得把它发到我们的故事里，因为他做了个动作，虽然这里放不了，

1300
00:59:27.950 --> 00:59:28.990
but he goes like, ugh.
但他发出了那种声音，呃。

1301
00:59:29.510 --> 00:59:33.730
He has this huge reaction, and everyone's like, what was that?
他反应特别大，大家都在想，那是什么情况？

1302
00:59:34.210 --> 00:59:38.770
Well, Jim is going to do this really weird thing where, you know, Andy says, if Dwight
吉姆要做一件非常奇怪的事，安迪说，如果德怀特

1303
00:59:38.770 --> 00:59:40.130
did this, I'm going to fire him.
做了这件事，我就要开除他。

1304
00:59:40.270 --> 00:59:46.230
Like, this is bigger than just Christmas bonuses, to which now Jim has to backpedal and sort of
这事儿比圣诞奖金严重多了，吉姆现在不得不退缩，然后

1305
00:59:46.230 --> 00:59:47.930
maybe say, maybe he did it.
也许会说，可能真是他干的。

1306
00:59:47.990 --> 00:59:48.610
He can't remember.
他不记得了。

1307
00:59:48.730 --> 00:59:49.590
It's coming back to him.
他慢慢想起来了。

1308
00:59:49.670 --> 00:59:51.010
Maybe he was the one who did it.
也许确实是他干的。

1309
00:59:51.150 --> 00:59:52.170
Everyone's so confused.
大家都困惑极了。

1310
00:59:52.850 --> 00:59:56.830
Dwight is now going to burst in the conference room in true Dwight fashion.
德怀特现在要以他特有的方式冲进会议室。

1311
00:59:56.830 --> 01:00:00.570
He is going to throw someone's iPod into the trash.
他要把某人的iPod扔进垃圾桶。

1312
01:00:00.630 --> 01:00:02.730
He is done with that Christmas music.
他受够了那些圣诞音乐。

1313
01:00:02.910 --> 01:00:07.950
He's going to put his boombox on the table and knock over all the cups and everything.
他要把音箱重重地放在桌上，撞倒所有的杯子和杂物。

1314
01:00:08.190 --> 01:00:09.990
I mean, why couldn't he just place it on the table?
我是说，他为什么就不能轻轻地放桌上呢？

1315
01:00:10.110 --> 01:00:17.190
But no, he makes this big statement and hits play, and I loved this scene.
但他没有，他搞出这么大动静然后按下播放键，我太喜欢这一幕了。

1316
01:00:17.510 --> 01:00:18.570
This is so great.
这真是太棒了。

1317
01:00:18.690 --> 01:00:23.490
This is going to set off a big montage of gift giving, and there's going to be a lot of rocking
这引出了一段很长的送礼蒙太奇，大家会在

1318
01:00:23.490 --> 01:00:24.730
out in the conference room.
会议室里疯狂摇滚。

1319
01:00:24.730 --> 01:00:28.190
Yes, a lot of air guitar, very aggressive air guitar.
没错，大量的空气吉他，非常狂野的空气吉他。

1320
01:00:28.810 --> 01:00:31.050
We had a fan question for Maddie S.
我们收到一个粉丝提问，来自阿肯色州拉塞尔维尔的Maddie S.

1321
01:00:31.190 --> 01:00:33.610
in Russellville, Arkansas, who asked,
她问，

1322
01:00:33.830 --> 01:00:37.550
how much did it cost to play Trans-Siberian Orchestra for this episode?
这一集播放跨西伯利亚管弦乐团的音乐花了多少钱？

1323
01:00:37.550 --> 01:00:44.030
I love TSO and love Dwight jamming out to this song, but the nerdy side of me has to wonder
我喜欢TSO，也喜欢德怀特跟着这首歌疯狂摇摆，但我书呆子的一面不禁好奇，

1324
01:00:44.030 --> 01:00:48.570
how much it costs to use one of their most popular, well-known songs for this episode.
在这一集里使用他们最出名、最受欢迎的歌曲之一要花多少钱。

1325
01:00:49.070 --> 01:00:54.670
Well, Maddie, as you know, this song was Carol of the Bells by Trans-Siberian Orchestra,
嗯，Maddie，如你所知，这首歌是跨西伯利亚管弦乐团的《铃儿响叮当》，

1326
01:00:54.730 --> 01:00:58.950
and it cost us $40,000 to use this song on the show.
我们在节目中使用这首歌花了4万美元。

1327
01:00:59.210 --> 01:01:01.970
This song was scripted from the very beginning.
这首歌从一开始就写在剧本里了。

1328
01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:03.730
It was the only song we wanted.
这是我们唯一想要的歌。

1329
01:01:04.530 --> 01:01:09.450
Steve Burgess shared with me, though, that NBC had a deal with The Office where The Office
不过史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，NBC和《办公室》有个协议，所以《办公室》

1330
01:01:09.450 --> 01:01:12.910
only had to pay 12% of the song.
只需要支付这首歌费用的12%。

1331
01:01:12.910 --> 01:01:16.870
So we technically got this for only $4,800.
所以严格来说我们只花了4800美元。

1332
01:01:17.590 --> 01:01:17.890
Okay.
好吧。

1333
01:01:18.390 --> 01:01:22.190
But here's a fun fact about TSO, which I thought was kind of cool.
不过关于TSO有个有趣的事实，我觉得挺酷的。

1334
01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:28.290
They were the first major rock band to go straight to performing in theaters and arenas.
他们是第一个直接在剧院和体育馆演出的主流摇滚乐队。

1335
01:01:28.450 --> 01:01:30.570
They never played at, like, any clubs.
他们从没在什么小俱乐部演出过。

1336
01:01:30.710 --> 01:01:32.670
They were never anyone's opening act.
他们从来没给别人做过暖场嘉宾。

1337
01:01:32.830 --> 01:01:36.070
They just were, like, a big deal from the get-go.
他们从一开始就是大牌。

1338
01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:38.270
Headliner all the way.
一直都是领衔主演。

1339
01:01:38.910 --> 01:01:39.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1340
01:01:39.610 --> 01:01:42.230
Well, now we're going to have a montage of all the gifts.
好了，现在我们要看一段礼物蒙太奇。

1341
01:01:42.930 --> 01:01:45.790
Oscar is going to give Kevin a cookie jar.
奥斯卡要送给凯文一个饼干罐。

1342
01:01:45.890 --> 01:01:50.750
It's a woman, dark, cascading hair, a sort of strapless gown.
那是一个女人，深色长发，穿着露肩礼服。

1343
01:01:51.470 --> 01:01:51.950
Yes.
没错。

1344
01:01:51.950 --> 01:01:56.250
We had a fan question from Jessica in Rochester, New York, who says,
我们收到一个来自纽约州罗切斯特市杰西卡的粉丝提问，她说，

1345
01:01:56.410 --> 01:01:58.310
who is that supposed to be?
那个人物应该是谁？

1346
01:01:58.770 --> 01:02:00.730
Well, I went to the script, Jessica.
嗯，我查了剧本，杰西卡。

1347
01:02:00.730 --> 01:02:03.610
It was scripted as Sofia Vergara.
剧本里写的是索菲娅·维加拉。

1348
01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:04.950
Yeah, I saw that, too.
是啊，我也看到了。

1349
01:02:04.950 --> 01:02:06.430
That is who that is.
那就是她本人。

1350
01:02:06.990 --> 01:02:09.770
So I don't know if we made that or what.
所以我不知道那是我们制作的还是怎么回事。

1351
01:02:09.870 --> 01:02:14.190
I think it kind of looks like I've seen this cookie jar that is Marilyn Monroe.
我觉得它看起来有点像我见过的那种玛丽莲·梦露造型的饼干罐。

1352
01:02:15.010 --> 01:02:16.710
That's what it looked like to me, too.
我也觉得看起来像那个。

1353
01:02:16.730 --> 01:02:18.110
And maybe they painted the hair.
而且他们可能把头发给涂了颜色。

1354
01:02:18.890 --> 01:02:19.370
Yes.
是的。

1355
01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:19.730
Yeah.
没错。

1356
01:02:20.630 --> 01:02:23.870
Meredith is going to give Jim a brochure for vasectomies.
梅雷迪思打算给吉姆一份输精管结扎手术的宣传册。

1357
01:02:24.630 --> 01:02:25.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1358
01:02:25.390 --> 01:02:29.590
Ryan and Kelly give Angela a T-shirt that says, ask, then touch.
瑞安和凯莉送给安吉拉一件T恤，上面写着“先问，再碰”。

1359
01:02:29.970 --> 01:02:31.690
She's so delighted by this.
她对此感到非常高兴。

1360
01:02:31.690 --> 01:02:36.010
Meanwhile, the air guitar is getting really heated.
与此同时，空气吉他大赛正进行得如火如荼。

1361
01:02:36.390 --> 01:02:38.470
It is Nate, Dwight, and Creed.
参赛者是内特、德怀特和克里德。

1362
01:02:38.770 --> 01:02:40.070
Then Gabe joins in.
然后盖博也加入了。

1363
01:02:40.430 --> 01:02:42.830
When Creed joins in, it's so perfect.
当克里德加入时，那场面真是太完美了。

1364
01:02:42.830 --> 01:02:43.930
It's my favorite thing.
这是我最喜欢的部分。

1365
01:02:44.310 --> 01:02:45.070
So good.
太棒了。

1366
01:02:45.310 --> 01:02:46.410
So much fun.
太有趣了。

1367
01:02:46.630 --> 01:02:50.370
I could have watched this montage for a longer period of time, I must say.
我必须说，这段剪辑我可以看更久。

1368
01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:54.050
During this montage, there is a fantastic scene.
在这段剪辑中，有一个非常精彩的场景。

1369
01:02:54.210 --> 01:02:58.410
It's in the deleted scenes where Meredith makes a play for Robert.
那是删减片段里的，梅雷迪思向罗伯特发起攻势。

1370
01:02:58.410 --> 01:02:59.650
It's so good.
真的太精彩了。

1371
01:03:00.070 --> 01:03:04.290
He's just kind of gazing at the Christmas tree, lost in thought.
他当时正盯着圣诞树，陷入了沉思。

1372
01:03:04.450 --> 01:03:08.710
She saddles up next to him and says, I see you're a little down.
她凑到他身边说：“我看你有点情绪低落。”

1373
01:03:08.950 --> 01:03:10.650
And he says, I am.
他说：“确实。”

1374
01:03:10.790 --> 01:03:11.430
I'm a mess.
“我一团糟。”

1375
01:03:11.650 --> 01:03:15.870
And Meredith says, how about I fix you some warm milk with some bourbon?
梅雷迪思说：“要不我给你热杯牛奶，加点波本威士忌？”

1376
01:03:16.290 --> 01:03:18.810
And Robert says, oh, that sounds nice.
罗伯特说：“哦，听起来不错。”

1377
01:03:19.190 --> 01:03:23.090
And then Meredith says, maybe watch a movie under a blanket.
然后梅雷迪思说：“或许我们可以盖着毯子看场电影。”

1378
01:03:23.570 --> 01:03:25.490
Robert goes, lovely.
罗伯特说：“太好了。”

1379
01:03:26.050 --> 01:03:31.630
Then he kind of comes to, and he says, wait, where is this taking place?
然后他回过神来，问道：“等等，这要在哪儿进行？”

1380
01:03:31.850 --> 01:03:34.850
And Meredith says, the Murphy bed in my basement.
梅雷迪思说：“在我地下室的墨菲床上。”

1381
01:03:35.050 --> 01:03:37.330
And then Robert is snapped back to reality.
然后罗伯特瞬间回到了现实。

1382
01:03:37.770 --> 01:03:39.770
He's like, what is happening to me?
他心想：我这是怎么了？

1383
01:03:40.130 --> 01:03:42.210
He rejects her advances.
他拒绝了她的示好。

1384
01:03:42.210 --> 01:03:46.470
And he says, I sincerely hope you find a sexual partner tonight.
他说：“我真诚地希望你今晚能找到性伴侣。”

1385
01:03:49.130 --> 01:03:50.210
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1386
01:03:50.350 --> 01:03:52.270
Robert California only says what he really means.
罗伯特·加利福尼亚只会说他真心实意的话。

1387
01:03:52.270 --> 01:03:55.090
So he really does sincerely hope.
所以他是真的真诚地希望她能找到。

1388
01:03:55.390 --> 01:03:57.690
It's not going to be him, but he wishes her well.
虽然那个人不会是他，但他祝她好运。

1389
01:03:58.310 --> 01:04:01.210
There's a scene in the annex that is one of my faves.
办公区有个场景是我最喜欢的片段之一。

1390
01:04:01.850 --> 01:04:03.710
Mindy Kaling just crushes it.
敏迪·卡灵演得太绝了。

1391
01:04:04.090 --> 01:04:06.330
Ryan and Kelly are on Kelly's computer.
瑞安和凯莉正在用凯莉的电脑。

1392
01:04:06.470 --> 01:04:07.510
She has a lot of viruses.
她的电脑里有很多病毒。

1393
01:04:07.830 --> 01:04:09.270
You don't really know what the scene is about.
你其实看不出那个场景到底在演什么。

1394
01:04:09.790 --> 01:04:12.910
Aaron walks in and says, game on.
亚伦走进来，说了句：“比赛开始。”

1395
01:04:13.090 --> 01:04:18.210
And oh my gosh, Mindy's shift as Kelly, where she's just like on it.
天哪，敏迪饰演的凯莉那种状态，她简直完全进入了角色。

1396
01:04:19.070 --> 01:04:22.970
And what that means is that Kelly is going to take down Jessica.
那意味着凯莉要对付杰西卡了。

1397
01:04:23.750 --> 01:04:25.870
So we've got Phyllis, Angela, and Oscar.
所以我们有菲利斯、安吉拉和奥斯卡。

1398
01:04:26.170 --> 01:04:28.790
She did the thing where you walk up laughing.
她做了那个走过来大笑的动作。

1399
01:04:29.290 --> 01:04:30.930
That's what I was going to say.
我正想说这个。

1400
01:04:31.010 --> 01:04:32.110
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1401
01:04:32.110 --> 01:04:33.310
It was scripted.
这是写在剧本里的。

1402
01:04:33.550 --> 01:04:39.970
It says that Kelly approaches, joins in on the laughter, and then says her line,
剧本上写着凯莉走过来，加入大家的笑声，然后说了这句台词，

1403
01:04:40.110 --> 01:04:41.210
Jessica, did you fart?
杰西卡，你放屁了吗？

1404
01:04:41.530 --> 01:04:43.110
It is like the record scratch.
就像唱片突然停顿了一样。

1405
01:04:43.290 --> 01:04:44.050
Everyone's like, uh.
每个人都一脸尴尬。

1406
01:04:45.050 --> 01:04:46.570
Jenna, we could not get through this.
珍娜，我们当时根本演不下去。

1407
01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:49.190
And I thought there'd be some on the bloopers.
我以为花絮里会有一些片段。

1408
01:04:49.370 --> 01:04:50.530
I know they're out there somewhere.
我知道它们肯定在某个地方存着。

1409
01:04:51.290 --> 01:04:53.290
We kept getting so tickled.
我们当时一直忍不住笑场。

1410
01:04:53.570 --> 01:04:56.670
But anyway, she's like, Jessica, did you fart?
但不管怎样，她当时说的是，杰西卡，你放屁了吗？

1411
01:04:56.810 --> 01:04:59.770
And then it cuts immediately to a Kelly talking head.
然后镜头立刻切到了凯莉的个人采访。

1412
01:04:59.770 --> 01:05:03.150
And she goes, and that is how it's done.
她说，这就是搞定它的方式。

1413
01:05:03.550 --> 01:05:05.390
And I loved that talking head.
我超爱那个采访片段。

1414
01:05:05.730 --> 01:05:11.250
There was an alt Kelly talking head here where she has a little bit more to say
这里原本还有一个凯莉的备选采访片段，她说了更多

1415
01:05:11.250 --> 01:05:14.330
about her strategy of taking someone down.
关于她如何打击别人的策略。

1416
01:05:14.370 --> 01:05:15.910
And it goes like this.
内容是这样的。

1417
01:05:16.330 --> 01:05:18.430
You don't want to get too clever with a takedown.
你不想在打击别人时显得太聪明。

1418
01:05:18.610 --> 01:05:21.430
When I was younger, I would overthink a mean comment.
我年轻的时候，会过度思考一句刻薄的话。

1419
01:05:21.590 --> 01:05:22.770
Get precious with it.
把它搞得太矫情。

1420
01:05:22.910 --> 01:05:27.570
But over time, I've learned you just want your insult to be simple, direct, relatable,
但随着时间推移，我学会了你的侮辱要简单、直接、容易产生共鸣，

1421
01:05:27.570 --> 01:05:29.310
and then you want to move on.
然后你就可以继续做别的事了。

1422
01:05:30.450 --> 01:05:31.430
She's not wrong.
她说得没错。

1423
01:05:32.230 --> 01:05:33.650
That's her full philosophy.
这就是她的完整哲学。

1424
01:05:34.230 --> 01:05:38.370
Well, you know, there's been a few times you and I have talked about where we're like,
嗯，你知道，我们聊过几次，当时我们都在想，

1425
01:05:38.890 --> 01:05:40.570
huh, Jim hasn't brought up Pam.
咦，吉姆怎么没提帕姆？

1426
01:05:40.790 --> 01:05:42.730
We haven't heard anything about Pam and the kids.
我们没听到任何关于帕姆和孩子们的消息。

1427
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:44.190
It's where it's Pam and the kids.
就是关于帕姆和孩子们的事。

1428
01:05:44.970 --> 01:05:46.290
There was a scene.
其实有个场景。

1429
01:05:46.490 --> 01:05:49.810
It's in deleted scenes where Jim receives a package.
在删减片段里，吉姆收到一个包裹。

1430
01:05:50.630 --> 01:05:53.950
Aaron very loudly and drunkly says, hey, you got a package.
亚伦很大声且醉醺醺地说，嘿，你有个包裹。

1431
01:05:54.130 --> 01:05:55.390
Do you want me to put it on your desk?
要我帮你放到桌上吗？

1432
01:05:55.570 --> 01:05:56.890
And he says, sure.
他说，好的。

1433
01:05:57.270 --> 01:06:01.450
Aaron throws it across the room and hits Kathy with it.
亚伦把包裹扔过房间，正好砸中了凯西。

1434
01:06:02.410 --> 01:06:06.650
And then it cuts to Jim opening the package and the package is from Pam.
然后镜头切到吉姆打开包裹，包裹是帕姆寄来的。

1435
01:06:07.750 --> 01:06:10.590
There's a card that says season greetings on the outside.
外面有一张卡片，写着节日问候。

1436
01:06:10.830 --> 01:06:16.450
And when you open it on the inside, Pam wrote, Cece heard there was a tree at work.
当你打开它时，里面写着，西西听说公司有棵树。

1437
01:06:16.690 --> 01:06:17.630
Love, Pam.
爱你的，帕姆。

1438
01:06:17.630 --> 01:06:20.730
And it is a very cute homemade ornament.
那是一个非常可爱的自制装饰品。

1439
01:06:21.110 --> 01:06:22.750
This is how the ornament was described.
剧本里是这样描述那个装饰品的。

1440
01:06:22.990 --> 01:06:25.510
A homemade ornament made out of colored construction paper.
一个用彩色手工纸做的自制装饰品。

1441
01:06:25.910 --> 01:06:30.470
It's a star with dried macaroni and beans and glitter on it.
那是一颗星星，上面粘着干通心粉、豆子和亮粉。

1442
01:06:31.070 --> 01:06:33.210
Jim smiles and hangs it on the tree.
吉姆笑了笑，把它挂在了树上。

1443
01:06:33.750 --> 01:06:40.670
Well, that would have gone to their tradition of exchanging homemade holiday gifts at the
嗯，那本来可以延续他们交换自制节日礼物的传统，就在

1444
01:06:40.670 --> 01:06:41.730
Dunder Mifflin party.
邓德·米夫林的派对上。

1445
01:06:41.730 --> 01:06:42.170
I know.
我知道。

1446
01:06:42.350 --> 01:06:43.130
That's their little tradition.
那是他们的小传统。

1447
01:06:43.350 --> 01:06:44.970
I thought I missed the scene.
我还以为我错过了那个场景。

1448
01:06:44.970 --> 01:06:48.430
And we talk about sometimes in deleted scenes, oh, maybe it should have been in, maybe it
我们有时会讨论删减片段，噢，也许它应该保留，也许

1449
01:06:48.430 --> 01:06:48.730
shouldn't.
不应该。

1450
01:06:48.830 --> 01:06:49.590
I liked it.
我很喜欢它。

1451
01:06:50.690 --> 01:06:55.030
Aaron approaches the bar for more alcohol, but Robert thinks maybe she needs to take
亚伦走向吧台想再喝点酒，但罗伯特觉得她或许该去

1452
01:06:55.030 --> 01:06:55.450
a walk.
散散步。

1453
01:06:55.790 --> 01:07:01.490
He suggests Oscar take over as bartender, but oh my gosh, I mean, he hasn't tended bar
他建议让奥斯卡接手当酒保，但天哪，我是说，他已经有一年

1454
01:07:01.490 --> 01:07:01.830
in a year.
没调过酒了。

1455
01:07:01.890 --> 01:07:07.370
He's going to need, he needs a mortar and pestle, a muddler, some chocolate shaving, you know.
他会需要，他需要研钵和研杵、捣棒、一些巧克力碎屑之类的东西。

1456
01:07:07.970 --> 01:07:09.390
He's as a mixologiSt.
他可是个调酒师。

1457
01:07:10.070 --> 01:07:11.370
I love this moment.
我喜欢这一刻。

1458
01:07:11.370 --> 01:07:16.150
I looked in the shooting draft and it said, Oscar looks around excitedly to no one.
我查了拍摄剧本，上面写着：奥斯卡兴奋地四处张望，却没人在看他。

1459
01:07:16.610 --> 01:07:21.290
And then he would have had a talking head where he shared that for a little bit of time,
然后他本该有个访谈镜头，分享说他曾有一小段时间，

1460
01:07:21.450 --> 01:07:23.750
he bartended in the East Village in 1983.
在1983年于东村当过酒保。

1461
01:07:24.730 --> 01:07:26.370
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1462
01:07:26.530 --> 01:07:28.190
Oh, that's fun backstory.
噢，那真是个有趣的背景故事。

1463
01:07:29.170 --> 01:07:34.290
Well, Robert and Aaron go outside and they're sort of commiserating over their mutual broken
罗伯特和亚伦走到外面，他们正因彼此破碎的

1464
01:07:34.290 --> 01:07:34.770
hearts.
心而同病相怜。

1465
01:07:34.770 --> 01:07:38.590
And Andy is watching this from the conference room window.
安迪从会议室的窗户看着这一幕。

1466
01:07:39.010 --> 01:07:41.190
He's going to start to get a little jealous.
他开始有点嫉妒了。

1467
01:07:41.590 --> 01:07:42.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1468
01:07:42.110 --> 01:07:44.110
A little worried that maybe something's happening.
有点担心是不是发生了什么事。

1469
01:07:44.410 --> 01:07:44.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1470
01:07:45.010 --> 01:07:52.710
And once again, Mark, who plays Nate, just has the most subtle but awesome comedy bomb that
再一次，饰演内特的马克，抛出了一个最微妙但又绝妙的

1471
01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:53.270
he drops.
喜剧炸弹。

1472
01:07:53.510 --> 01:07:57.170
He just looks at Jessica and asks her how she does her makeup.
他只是看着杰西卡，问她是怎么化妆的。

1473
01:07:57.490 --> 01:07:58.650
How long does it take her?
要花多久时间？

1474
01:07:58.990 --> 01:08:02.630
These moments with him crack me up so much.
他这些时刻总是让我笑得不行。

1475
01:08:02.630 --> 01:08:04.710
And that was not scripted.
而且那不是剧本里写的。

1476
01:08:04.850 --> 01:08:05.550
Oh, no way.
噢，不会吧。

1477
01:08:05.930 --> 01:08:06.590
That was just Nate.
那完全是内特即兴发挥的。

1478
01:08:06.770 --> 01:08:06.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1479
01:08:07.050 --> 01:08:11.270
Because in the script, the only note is that Andy is looking out the window.
因为剧本里唯一的备注就是安迪在往窗外看。

1480
01:08:11.510 --> 01:08:12.970
So Mark improvised that?
所以那是马克即兴发挥的？

1481
01:08:13.230 --> 01:08:13.730
Yes.
没错。

1482
01:08:13.850 --> 01:08:15.670
They had to just improvise some chit chat.
他们当时必须即兴聊点闲话。

1483
01:08:15.950 --> 01:08:17.170
That is amazing.
那太棒了。

1484
01:08:17.410 --> 01:08:20.070
And Eleanor's response is Jessica was perfect.
而埃莉诺的回答很完美，杰西卡。

1485
01:08:20.530 --> 01:08:21.190
I know.
我知道。

1486
01:08:21.590 --> 01:08:26.310
Well, in the bullpen, Toby is really boring Val by talking about Chad Flinderman.
在办公区，托比一直在聊查德·弗林德曼，让瓦尔觉得非常无聊。

1487
01:08:26.650 --> 01:08:31.290
I was curious if there was more to this moment right before Daryl walks in.
我很好奇在达里尔走进来之前，这一幕是否还有更多内容。

1488
01:08:31.290 --> 01:08:36.350
So I went to the script, and it says, Toby is by Val, who looks really bored.
